.oh-my-zsh/

# Machine-specific kanshi profiles — monitor make/model/serial must not land in this
# public repo. Stowed alongside the tracked skeleton, which `include`s them.
# The directory stays tracked via 00-placeholder.conf, which must be a REAL .conf and not a
# .gitkeep: kanshi hard-errors when the include glob matches nothing, and `*` does not match a
# dot-prefixed name — so a .gitkeep left kanshi refusing to start at all. See that file.
config-stow/kanshi/kanshi/config.d/*
!config-stow/kanshi/kanshi/config.d/00-placeholder.conf

# Machine-/device-specific niri overrides — real output blocks, custom xkb keymap path,
# Bluetooth device MAC binds. Optionally `include`d by the tracked config.kdl skeleton;
# supplied per-machine (or by the private machine-config repo). Same reasoning as kanshi.
config-stow/niri/.config/niri/local.kdl
